   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of constituents to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Skills Passport adopted by Sri Lanka in 2020

New services provided to Migrant Workers through digitalisation of existing Recognition of Prior Learning system and enrolment of Migrant Workers in the National Skills Passport initiative for job matching with employers

The ITUC Recruitment Advisor (RA) has been launched in Sri Lanka in December 2020, along with translations into the two local languages. The platform enables migrant workers to review their recruitment experience and access information about relevant legislations in Sri Lanka and countries of destination. An online complaints mechanisms supported by civil society has also been launched in Sri Lanka. The launch event was attended by 2,400 people. The MRA Sri Lanka Facebook page has 12,304 followers; 3,618 web users have accessed the platforms, and 296 Migrant Workers have submitted reviews of recruitment agencies (offline). Technical and financial assistance to Technical and Vocational Education Commission (Ministry of Skills Development) to digitalise skills assessment and recognition system
Employers Federation of Ceylon supported to expand the National Skills Passport system to include Migrant Workers. ILO specifically provides technical support for designing the system, software development, improvement of ITC infrastructure, awareness and institutional capacity building. 
 
ILO contribution ideas: ILO, with support of the European Union, has provided technical support in the establishment of the Recruitment Advisor website. ILO reviewed the contents of the page and MRA standard to ensure it aligns with ILS. 
Three Sri Lankan Trade Unions affiliated with ITUC - Sri Lanka Nidahas Sevaka Sangamaya  (SLNSS), Ceylon Workers Congress (CWC) &amp; National Trade Union Federation (NTUF) were capacitated to continue operations of Recruitment Advisor web pages for Sri Lanka. At present, the SLNSS is designated and facilitated to manage the RA Facebook and RA national webpages. Accordingly, the SLNSS was capacitated to establish linkages with Migration Forum Asia (MFA) and its local affiliates under Hamsa initiative. Furthermore, technical and resource assistance provided to the trade unions for a public outreach to promote public awareness of RA and its services to migrant workers and their families.</narrative>
   </description>
